<section class="lumen-section lumen-section--yellow" id="panels">
  <div class="lumen-container">
    <span class="lumen-eyebrow">01 / Service work</span>
    <h2 style="max-width:18ch;margin-bottom:2rem">Panels. <em>Heavy-up.</em> Re-bus.</h2>

    <div class="lumen-services">
      <article class="lumen-service">
        <div class="lumen-service-num">A</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3>200A panel upgrade</h3>
          <p>100A or 150A → 200A main panel (Siemens or Square D QO). Includes new meter socket if needed, whole-house surge protection, grounding upgrade, permit, inspection sign-off.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$2,800 – $4,400</span>
      </article>
      <article class="lumen-service">
        <div class="lumen-service-num">B</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3>Federal Pacific / Zinsco re-bus</h3>
          <p>Insurance-driven swap of unsafe legacy panels with the SAME 200A service entry. New panel + breakers + service to the meter. No service-size change.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$2,200 – $3,400</span>
      </article>
      <article class="lumen-service">
        <div class="lumen-service-num">C</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3>Subpanel install</h3>
          <p>Detached garage, ADU, finished basement. 60A&ndash;100A subpanel with main lug or main breaker, fed from main service.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$1,400 – $2,800</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lumen-section" id="ev">
  <div class="lumen-container">
    <span class="lumen-eyebrow">02 / EV chargers</span>
    <h2 style="max-width:18ch;margin-bottom:2rem">Level 2. <em>Done right.</em></h2>

    <div class="lumen-services">
      <article class="lumen-service">
        <div class="lumen-service-num">D</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3>Hardwired Level 2 (40A)</h3>
          <p>Tesla Wall Connector, ChargePoint Home Flex, or owner-supplied. Dedicated 50A breaker, #6 copper, hardwire to charger. Load calc verified before quote.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$1,100 – $1,800</span>
      </article>
      <article class="lumen-service">
        <div class="lumen-service-num">E</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3>NEMA 14-50 outlet (40A)</h3>
          <p>For portable / unhardwired chargers. Dedicated 50A breaker, GFCI-protected outlet, weather-resistant if outdoor.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$950 – $1,500</span>
      </article>
      <article class="lumen-service">
        <div class="lumen-service-num">F</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3>Dual EV install</h3>
          <p>Two chargers from one service. Load-share device or dedicated 100A subpanel for the garage. Often required for households with 2+ EVs.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$2,400 – $3,800</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lumen-section lumen-section--black" id="rewire">
  <div class="lumen-container">
    <span class="lumen-eyebrow">03 / Rewires &amp; troubleshooting</span>
    <h2 style="max-width:18ch;margin-bottom:2rem">Knob &amp; tube. <em>Aluminum.</em> Mystery.</h2>

    <div class="lumen-services">
      <article class="lumen-service" style="border-top-color:#FFFFFF">
        <div class="lumen-service-num" style="color:#FFFFFF">G</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3 style="color:#FFFFFF">Whole-home rewire (1,200&ndash;2,000 sq ft)</h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88)">Pull every legacy circuit, run new Romex through accessible attic/basement/walls. Code-current outlets, AFCI/GFCI as required. Drywall-minimal fishing where construction allows.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$14,000 – $28,000</span>
      </article>
      <article class="lumen-service" style="border-top-color:#FFFFFF">
        <div class="lumen-service-num" style="color:#FFFFFF">H</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3 style="color:#FFFFFF">Aluminum-branch remediation (CO/ALR or AlumiConn)</h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88)">Replace every receptacle and switch in an aluminum-wired home with code-listed copper-pigtailed devices. Insurance-acceptable alternative to full rewire.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$2,800 – $5,400</span>
      </article>
      <article class="lumen-service" style="border-top-color:#FFFFFF">
        <div class="lumen-service-num" style="color:#FFFFFF">I</div>
        <div class="lumen-service-body">
          <h3 style="color:#FFFFFF">Diagnostic / troubleshooting</h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88)">Hourly. Tracking down a flickering light, a tripping breaker, a dead circuit, an unknown wire. Includes the time to diagnose AND the time to fix unless parts are needed.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="lumen-service-tag">$140 / hour</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

